From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:19:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Open a pasted path in the file dialog with Ctrl+V

Ctrl+V in a file dialog, outside a text box, takes the path from the
clipboard: the first line, without surrounding whitespace or quotes,
with "~" as the home folder and file:// URIs decoded. In an open-file
dialog an existing file opens at once, as if selected and opened. An
existing folder is shown. The save dialog never saves: a folder is
shown, and a file path shows its folder and puts the name in the file
name box. Anything else (a missing path, a relative path, other text)
opens the location box with that text selected, replacing the old path.

Ctrl+L and the edit button now open the location box with the path
selected, so typing or pasting replaces it, as in GTK file choosers and
browsers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

